            },
            "margin_authority": "GF-5 transformer SOP rev C: if reconstructed k_WmK >= 0.12 AND THW SNR >= 8.0, continue-idle of bay B-7 is forbidden even if Thwveil reports 0.024 W/mK. Hall ESD is a different gate. Kill tripwire is 0.80 W/mK.",
        },
        "proposed_action": {
            "actor": "night transformer operator Calum Dyer, citing Thwveil 0.024 W/mK and a quiet heater channel",
            "summary": "continue B-7 recirc idle; 40.00 W is preamp heater noise on a healthy oil last-good",
            "basis_claimed": "Thwveil is the only OEM THW SoT and a night abort of B-7 is a bay-nomination miss",
        },
        "safety_decision": {
            "decision": "REJECT",
            "rationale": "Continue-idle is refused. Serialized reconstruction: k_WmK = k_w * (P / dT) = 0.10 * (40.00 / 20.00) = 0.20, which is 0.08 W/mK over the 0.12 isolate floor and 0.60 W/mK under the 0.80 hall-kill tripwire, and THW SNR is 12.0 >= 8.0. P/dT identity 40.00 / 20.00 = 2.00; heat-rate identity Q = k * G * dT = 0.20 * 10.00 * 20.00 = 40.00 W. Permit clock was slid 40.00 s and vendor THW packets were dropped, so Thwveil is a collusion party (THW vendor plus operator plus permit clerk Odette Marsh). Ordered: refuse continue-idle now. Scope: this REJECT does not ESD the transformer hall (that is the companion question) and does not isolate the oil dT sensor.",
            "threshold": "k_WmK>=0.12 AND thw_snr>=8.0 => refuse continue-idle; Thwveil is not SoT; hall-kill if k_WmK>=0.80",
            "stated_residuals": "recirc-hold still required to hold the 0.20 W/mK; 0.20 vs a true 0.80 kill is a production cut; Thwveil remains the only OEM THW channel",
        },
        "executed_action": {
